 "posture": "Breadth sits at 51.4/100 (Neutral, 60-75% equity band): the rally is neither broad nor broken - 38 of the 75 tracked names hold their 200-day average but only 27 remain above the 50-day. VIX at 19.3 is normal-to-cautious, and price risk is now concentrated in AI/semis as the mega-cap complex digests the Nvidia leadership shock rather than in the index itself. The 10-year at 5.15% with BofA now calling December-January-March hikes keeps valuation pressure on long-duration growth. Crypto is neutral (50.9/100) but internally soft: BTC 30.7% below its 1-year high, only 26% of alts above their 200DMA, and a near-total 30-day momentum washout. Stance: keep the core, let new-money entries wait for a 50-day breadth reclaim, and avoid adding leveraged duration on either side.",
 "sentiment": "Risk-off and internally split: mega-cap AI leadership cracked (NVDA -12.8% on the week) while Friday breadth was actually positive and defensives held - a rotation, not yet a broad liquidation. Fear gauges are stretched (crypto Fear & Greed ~19) and a hawkish Fed caps any rebound.",
